messages "mangla**To: exosSubj: about areasCc: silas haplo sauron mangla airborne zathrasDate: Oct 12Hmmm A mentor has to look over the area then submit to archfor a 10 minute run through to make sure it fits the place youwant to put it and has not obvoius spelling or exit errors.Then if it looks like the theme fits in with the place thenewwiz and mentor were going to put it, then the newwiz ispromoted and the area placed in. If the newwiz goes directlyto an arch or another wiz then that is the personal choiceof the newwiz. The key to the whole thing is we do notwant newwiz areas in. (As has happened recently) and we do notwant poor areas that have not been check and have more errorsthan rooms to make it into the mud. Seems like common sense to me!-ManglaPS: As for Turbo, he wanted a fast approval and so I told him toget some other wizzes to go through it and give comments then hecould ask an arch to do the run through thing and wallah!**"
